<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongol conquest of the Jin dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from 1211</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongol conquest of the Jin dynasty was the series of campaigns from 1211 in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> and his successors destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> Jin state in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. The Jin capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhongdu">Zhongdu</a> fell in 1215, and the dynasty ended in 1234. The conquest brought northern China under Mongol rule, laying the base for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongol-conquest-of-the-jin-dynasty.jpg" alt="Mongol conquest of the Jin dynasty" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sayf al-Vâhidî. Hérât. Afghanistan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_entre_mongols_%26_chinois_(1211).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
